校对: tpring
时间轴: T-boy

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
主教之争

5
00:00:40,651 --> 00:00:44,214
对菲奥娜麦格的关注持续增加
Growing concern for Fiona McGregor,

6
00:00:44,215 --> 00:00:47,181
这名英国护士在海湾国家库朗
the nurse held in the Gulf state of Kumran

7
00:00:47,216 --> 00:00:49,120
因持有一瓶威士忌被捕
for alleged possession of a bottle of whisky.

8
00:00:49,291 --> 00:00:51,727
被判10年徒刑和40下鞭刑
Her sentence of 10 years' imprisonment

9
00:00:51,728 --> 00:00:54,338
即将确认执行
and 40 lashes is awaiting confirmation.

10
00:00:54,373 --> 00:00:58,165
今天 她母亲偕同当地议员斯图尔特戈登
Today, her mother, accompanied by her MP, Stuart Gordon,

11
00:00:58,166 --> 00:00:59,752
和其他支持者
and a group of sympathisers,

12
00:00:59,787 --> 00:01:02,156
对库朗大使馆提交请愿书
took a petition to the Kumran embassy,

13
00:01:02,157 --> 00:01:04,526
但库朗拒绝接受
but the Kumrani's refused to accept it.

14
00:01:04,561 --> 00:01:08,250
外交大臣对此事表示遗憾
The Foreign Secretary described the incident as regrettable,

15
00:01:08,251 --> 00:01:10,465
但并未计划采取行动
but no action is planned.

16
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:11,731
关掉吧 伯纳
Turn it off, Bernard.

17
00:01:11,831 --> 00:01:14,282
今日英镑汇率仍然不妙
The Pound has a bad day

18
00:01:14,382 --> 00:01:17,160
真让人忧心 汉弗莱 公众同情情绪很强
This is very worrying. There's a lot of public sympathy.

19
00:01:17,371 --> 00:01:19,965
我肯定外交大臣会给您建议的
I'm sure the Foreign Secretary will advise you.

20
00:01:20,131 --> 00:01:22,352
他建议我袖手旁观
He advises me to do nothing.

21
00:01:22,353 --> 00:01:23,661
我肯定这是个好建议
I'm sure that's good advice.

22
00:01:25,331 --> 00:01:27,720
如果袖手旁观 我们会显得既无情 又无能
If we do nothing, we look heartless. And feeble.

23
00:01:27,891 --> 00:01:29,408
政府不可以同时
It doesn't do the government any good to

24
00:01:29,409 --> 00:01:31,817
显得既无情又无能
look heartless and feeble simultaneously.

25
00:01:32,753 --> 00:01:33,761
你说呢 伯纳?
What do you think, Bernard?

26
00:01:33,796 --> 00:01:35,189
不如想点办法
Perhaps you could arrange it

27
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:37,564
让您显得要么无情 要么无能?
so you only look heartless and feeble alternately.

28
00:01:38,731 --> 00:01:41,115
汉弗莱 我们得采取措施
Humphrey, we must do something.

29
00:01:41,116 --> 00:01:43,919
首相 库朗是英国的好朋友
Prime Minister, The Kumranis are good friends of Britain.

30
00:01:43,954 --> 00:01:46,043
在我国下大笔国防订单
They just placed a huge defence contract with us,

31
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:48,496
向我们通报苏联在伊拉克的动向
they tell us about the Soviets in Iraq,

32
00:01:48,651 --> 00:01:51,319
甚至为我们破坏石油输出国组织协定
they even sabotage OPEC agreements for us.

33
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,526
我们惹不起他们
We can't afford to upset them.

34
00:01:53,561 --> 00:01:54,251
我都知道 汉弗莱
I know, Humphrey,

35
00:01:54,252 --> 00:01:57,533
可一个英国国民要受酷刑了
but a British national is facing a barbaric punishment

36
00:01:57,568 --> 00:01:59,929
为在国外犯的一点小过失
for a trivial offence committed in a foreign country.

37
00:02:00,316 --> 00:02:02,329
外交部是保卫英国国民利益的
The Foreign Office is there to protect British nationals.

38
00:02:02,531 --> 00:02:04,812
是保卫英国国家利益的
They are there to protect British interests.

39
00:02:04,813 --> 00:02:06,363
挨鞭子可不符合她的利益
It's not in her interest to be flogged.

40
00:02:06,398 --> 00:02:08,210
救她也不符合我们的利益
It's not in ours to prevent it.

41
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:11,173
符合 这可能重创政府威信
This could hurt the government very badly.

42
00:02:11,208 --> 00:02:14,808
据我所知 明天外交大臣
Well, I understand that tomorrow the Foreign Secretary will

43
00:02:14,809 --> 00:02:17,713
将发出照会 严正抗议
deliver a strong note of protest to The Kumranis.

44
00:02:17,748 --> 00:02:18,560
干嘛不现在发?
Why can't he do it now?

45
00:02:18,561 --> 00:02:20,925
还没征求库朗同意呢
We haven't got their agreement yet.

46
00:02:22,276 --> 00:02:24,737
我们正在秘会大使
We're seeing the ambassador privately now.

47
00:02:24,738 --> 00:02:27,609
一旦他们接受了措辞 我们就发
Once they approve the wording, we hand it over.

48
00:02:27,744 --> 00:02:30,646
然后我们就仁至义尽了      真无情
Then we'll have done all we can.        Very heartless.

49
00:02:30,851 --> 00:02:33,240
无情总比无脑好
It's safer to be heartless than mindless.

50
00:02:33,411 --> 00:02:37,290
历史就是无情对无脑的胜利史
History is the triumph of the heartless over the mindless.

51
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:40,004
外交部休想让内阁同意这种政策
The Cabinet will never agree to this policy.

52
00:02:40,005 --> 00:02:43,893
外交部从未指望内阁同意他们任何政策
The F.O. never expect that for their policies.

53
00:02:44,816 --> 00:02:47,015
所以他们从不解释清楚
That's why they never fully explain them.

54
00:02:48,189 --> 00:02:49,807
甚至对外交大臣?
Even to the Foreign Secretary?

55
00:02:49,808 --> 00:02:52,006
尤其对外交大臣
Especially not to the Foreign Secretary.

56
00:02:52,999 --> 00:02:56,268
外交部只要求他们实施后
All that the Foreign Office requires is that the Cabinet

57
00:02:56,286 --> 00:02:59,239
内阁同意就行
agree to their decisionsonce once they've been taken.

58
00:02:59,274 --> 00:03:01,705
还有事吗 首相? 我约了人吃晚餐
Will that be all? Prime Minister,I have a dinner engagement.

59
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,914
好 没事了      首相
Yes, I suppose so.        Prime Minister

60
00:03:03,949 --> 00:03:07,029
今晚的招待会要开始了
It's time to get ready for the reception here this evening.

61
00:03:07,064 --> 00:03:11,041
谁要来?      英国圣公会代表
Oh, who's coming?        The synod of the Church of England.

62
00:03:11,076 --> 00:03:13,568
圣埃德蒙教区主教出缺了
There's a vacancy in Bury St Edmunds.

63
00:03:13,603 --> 00:03:17,216
每当重要主教出缺 他们就要来      为什么?
They come here when a bishopric is vacant.        Why?

64
00:03:17,653 --> 00:03:20,923
游说 有两个候选人 免得您选错
To lobby. So you don't choose the wrong name.

65
00:03:21,131 --> 00:03:23,273
我怎么知道该选谁?
How should I know which one to choose?

66
00:03:23,274 --> 00:03:25,878
像其他公务员决定一样 首相
It's like any Civil Service option.Prime Minister

67
00:03:25,913 --> 00:03:27,334
这是个纸牌戏法
It will be a conjuring trick.

68
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:31,672
随便抽张牌 总抽中
You know. Take any card, you always end up with

69
00:03:31,707 --> 00:03:34,220
魔术师要您抽的那张
the card the magician forced you to take.

70
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:36,797
要是我不抽呢?      您会抽的
Suppose I don't take it?        You will.

71
00:03:37,811 --> 00:03:40,344
都给我哪些牌?
Who are these cards I am supposed to choose?

72
00:03:40,379 --> 00:03:41,819
教会的牌
Well, With the Church,

73
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:44,184
不外乎是J(恶棍)或者Q(同性恋)
you usually get the choice of a knave or a queen.

74
00:03:49,169 --> 00:03:51,848
我们都很欢迎你回贝利参加晚宴
We do appreciate you dining at the college.

75
00:03:52,011 --> 00:03:55,080
与老朋友吃饭向来是我的荣幸
It is always a pleasure to dine with old friends.

76
00:03:55,081 --> 00:03:56,391
谢谢 院长
Thank you, Master.

77
00:03:56,426 --> 00:04:00,195
汉弗莱 我还有四五年就退休了
Humphrey, I'll be retiring in four or five years.

78
00:04:00,196 --> 00:04:03,340
你不也是吗?
Isn't that roughly when you retire from the civil service?

79
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:04,753
对
Yes.

80
00:04:04,788 --> 00:04:08,699
司库和我都觉得 你就是
The Bursar and I think you could be just the chap

81
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,916
继任贝利学院院长的合适人选
to succeed me as Master of Ballie.

82
00:04:11,406 --> 00:04:12,342
真的?
Really?

83
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:15,414
但还有一个障碍 教务长
But there is one obstacle. The Dean.

84
00:04:15,449 --> 00:04:16,606
他有什么意见?
Why is he an obstacle?

85
00:04:16,607 --> 00:04:18,462
他说你聪明过头了
He says you're too clever by half.

86
00:04:19,371 --> 00:04:21,377
我还以为在牛津
I should have thought that at Oxford

87
00:04:21,378 --> 00:04:24,230
说人聪明是赞誉呢
to be called clever might be rather a compliment.

88
00:04:24,531 --> 00:04:29,041
他还说你自鸣得意      多谢了 司库
He also says you're smug.        Thank you, Bursar.

89
00:04:29,076 --> 00:04:31,083
你有得是资本嘛
Well, you've got a lot to be smug about.

90
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:33,603
要是我也一年挣7万5
If I had 75,000 a year,

91
00:04:34,253 --> 00:04:36,567
有爵位 有物价指数化养老金
a knighthood, an index-linked pension,

92
00:04:37,055 --> 00:04:39,492
还有群政客专替我背黑锅
and a bunch of politicians to take the blame for

93
00:04:39,592 --> 00:04:41,564
我也会得意的
all my mistakes, I'd be pretty smug myself!

94
00:04:42,401 --> 00:04:44,195
教务长生怕
The Dean is paranoid that

95
00:04:44,196 --> 00:04:46,478
我们在背着他密谋此事
we're intriguing in this matter behind his back.

96
00:04:46,513 --> 00:04:49,811
所以我们决定...
That is why we decided to...

97
00:04:49,812 --> 00:04:52,146
趁他不在时跟你谈
discuss it with you while he's away.

98
00:04:52,181 --> 00:04:53,226
对 当然
Yes Quite.

99
00:04:53,451 --> 00:04:56,530
要让你当贝利院长
The only way you'll become Master of Baillie

100
00:04:56,531 --> 00:04:59,145
唯一办法是甩掉教务长
is if we can dump the Dean.

101
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:02,717
怎么甩?      不好办 他是个懒鬼
But how?        It isn't easy. He's a lazy devil.

102
00:05:02,752 --> 00:05:05,165
一周只用工作4小时
He only has to do four hours' work a week.

103
00:05:05,331 --> 00:05:07,777
上一堂课 几次辅导
Give one lecture and a couple of tutorials

104
00:05:07,778 --> 00:05:09,067
就享有终身教职
and he's got tenure for life!

105
00:05:09,891 --> 00:05:12,928
他只有两样爱好 板球和蒸汽机
Only two interests - cricket and steam engines.

106
00:05:13,131 --> 00:05:16,789
从不读一本新书 从没有一个新想法
Never reads a new book, never thinks a new thought.

107
00:05:16,824 --> 00:05:19,045
所以在牛津教书最合适不过了
So being an Oxford don is the perfect job.

108
00:05:21,181 --> 00:05:24,187
那什么才能把他调离贝利呢?
So what would get him away from Baillie?

109
00:05:24,222 --> 00:05:26,816
唯有主教职位      主教职位?
Only a bishopric.        A bishopric?

110
00:05:26,851 --> 00:05:30,458
我们在考虑圣埃德蒙
We wondered about Bury St Edmunds.

111
00:05:30,459 --> 00:05:32,261
正好出缺了 是吗?
That's up for grabs, isn't it?

112
00:05:32,296 --> 00:05:36,508
对 非常不错的教区 在上院占一席
Yes, a very agreeable diocese. It has a seat in the Lords.

113
00:05:36,543 --> 00:05:38,312
教务长一定喜欢
The Dean would like that.

114
00:05:38,313 --> 00:05:41,576
他第三大爱好是往贵族阶层爬
His third hobby is sucking up to the aristocracy.

115
00:05:42,411 --> 00:05:44,879
那当然 不过 这不由我作主
Naturally. Well, it's not up to me at all.

116
00:05:45,051 --> 00:05:48,639
教会想保持平衡
The Church wants to maintain the balance.

117
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,690
平衡什么?
What balance?

118
00:05:49,725 --> 00:05:52,561
信上帝和不信上帝的成员
Between those who believe in God and those who don't.

119
00:05:52,771 --> 00:05:55,649
教会还有不信上帝的成员?
Is there anyone in the Church who doesn't?

120
00:05:55,851 --> 00:05:58,041
有啊 大多数主教
Oh, yes. Most of the bishops.

121
00:05:59,329 --> 00:06:02,610
无论如何 圣埃德蒙已经有主了
But, in any case, Bury St Edmunds is all sewn up.

122
00:06:02,611 --> 00:06:04,718
归史丹弗教士
Canon Stanford is getting the job.

123
00:06:04,753 --> 00:06:06,930
我们以为要由首相选呢
We thought the Prime Minister had to choose.

124
00:06:07,131 --> 00:06:09,929
对 可他们另一个候选人没指望
But they gave an impossible second candidate.

125
00:06:10,091 --> 00:06:11,608
再说
In any case,

126
00:06:11,609 --> 00:06:14,796
教务长的公职资历不足
the Dean hasn't done enough public service to qualify.

127
00:06:15,051 --> 00:06:17,519
还有哪个教区出缺吗?
Are any other dioceses coming free?

128
00:06:17,731 --> 00:06:20,120
唉 这种事不常有
Well, it doesn't happen very often.

129
00:06:20,291 --> 00:06:24,073
年纪大的都不必60岁退休
The older appointees don't have to retire at 60.

130
00:06:24,074 --> 00:06:25,887
主教通常很长寿
Bishops tend to have long lives.

131
00:06:25,922 --> 00:06:28,726
显然上帝不急着召他们去陪他
Apparently the Lord isn't all that keen for them to join Him

132
00:06:30,931 --> 00:06:36,300
你觉得教务长需要哪种公职资历?
What sort of public service did you have in mind for the Dean

133
00:06:36,335 --> 00:06:41,437
何不让主教派他去库朗
Well, why don't you get the bishop to send him to Kumran,

134
00:06:41,472 --> 00:06:45,194
去为那个护士说情呢?
to try to intercede on behalf of that nurse?

135
00:06:45,306 --> 00:06:49,604
阿拉伯人喜欢他 他是伊斯兰教专家
The Arabs love him because he's an expert in Islamic studies

136
00:06:49,639 --> 00:06:53,435
他也喜欢阿拉伯人 横竖我们不吃亏
He'd love the Arabs. Either way, we can't lose.

137
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:55,080
对呀
That's right.

138
00:06:55,651 --> 00:06:58,233
如果他失败 他尽力了
If he fails, at least he's tried.

139
00:06:58,234 --> 00:07:00,130
如果他成功 他就是英雄
If he succeeds, he's a hero.

140
00:07:00,131 --> 00:07:02,428
如果他回不来 也没人想念他
And if he doesn't come back, he won't be missed.

141
00:07:04,371 --> 00:07:06,965
多可怕的国家啊
No, it's such an awful country.

142
00:07:07,131 --> 00:07:09,369
偷东西要砍手
They cut people's hands off and

143
00:07:09,370 --> 00:07:12,581
女人一通奸 就要被砸死
women get stoned when they commit adultery.

144
00:07:12,616 --> 00:07:13,202
不像英国
Unlike Britain where

145
00:07:13,203 --> 00:07:14,900
她们喝到醉死 然后去通奸
they commit adultery when they get stoned

146
00:07:20,813 --> 00:07:24,571
他可能丢几个零件再回来呢
He may even come back with a few parts missing!

147
00:07:25,651 --> 00:07:27,500
瞧 手没了
Look, no hands!

148
00:07:31,571 --> 00:07:33,841
抱歉犹豫这么久 彼得
Sorry to be so hesitant, Peter.

149
00:07:33,842 --> 00:07:35,671
我从没委任过主教
I've never appointed a bishop before.

150
00:07:35,706 --> 00:07:40,075
是向女王推荐委任 首相
recommended the appointment to the sovereign, PM

151
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:43,853
对 给我讲讲史丹弗教士
Yes. Tell me about Canon Stanford.

152
00:07:43,888 --> 00:07:48,027
好的 麦克名望很高 他是个现代派
Well, Mike is very highly thought of. He's a modernist.

153
00:07:48,062 --> 00:07:50,644
现代派?      神学术语 首相
Modernist?        A theological term. Prime Minister

154
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:51,919
他似乎认为
It seems that he accepts that

155
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,519
圣经里某些事不能照字面理解
some events described in the Bible are not literally true.

156
00:07:55,554 --> 00:07:58,356
他认为那些是比喻 神话或传奇故事
He sees them as metaphors, myths or legends.

157
00:07:58,391 --> 00:08:02,480
他只关注它们的精神或哲学涵义
He's interested in their spiritual and philosophical truth.

158
00:08:02,515 --> 00:08:05,012
你是说他不信七日创世
He doesn't believe the world was made in seven days

159
00:08:05,013 --> 00:08:07,290
夏娃是亚当肋骨这一套?
and Eve came out of Adam's rib?

160
00:08:07,325 --> 00:08:12,035
正是 首相      貌似挺明智的 还有呢?
Precisely.        Sounds very sensible. Anything else?

161
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:16,399
他上过温彻斯特和牛津新学院
He went to Winchester and New College, Oxford,

162
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,987
他是首选
and his name is first on the list.

163
00:08:18,022 --> 00:08:21,263
好像不错      他夫人也极其合适
Sounds good.        And he has an eminently suitable wife.

164
00:08:21,298 --> 00:08:23,440
你是说她虔诚 广做善事?
Devout, full of good works?

165
00:08:24,524 --> 00:08:27,388
不 我是说她是奇切斯特伯爵的女儿
No, I mean she's the daughter of the Earl of Chichester.

166
00:08:29,769 --> 00:08:32,187
明白了 第二位呢?
I see. And what about the second?

167
00:08:32,851 --> 00:08:37,138
第二位是保罗哈维博士
Well, second is Doctor Paul Harvey.

168
00:08:38,293 --> 00:08:39,115
怎样?
And?

169
00:08:39,150 --> 00:08:42,474
他是个可敬的人      然而?
He's an admirable man.        But?

170
00:08:43,879 --> 00:08:45,703
当然 您来拿主意 首相
It's your choice, of course, Prime Minister

171
00:08:45,738 --> 00:08:47,845
可人们怀疑
but there's a suspicion

172
00:08:47,846 --> 00:08:50,725
他倾向于政教分离主义
he tends towards disestablishmentarianism.

173
00:08:52,851 --> 00:08:54,531
什么?
What?

174
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,899
认为圣公会
The view that the Church of England

175
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,387
不该成为国家政权的一部分
shouldn't be part of the state.

176
00:09:00,451 --> 00:09:02,469
有些人觉得该把它们分离出去
Some people feel it should be separate,

177
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:04,219
像卫理公会和天主教会一样
like Methodists or Catholics.

178
00:09:04,405 --> 00:09:07,226
他们说老百姓觉得国教只是
They think ordinary people feel the established church is

179
00:09:07,227 --> 00:09:10,130
统治阶级的俱乐部,而不是信仰
a club for the ruling classes. Not a faith

180
00:09:10,165 --> 00:09:11,242
听起来人不错啊
Sounds a good man.

181
00:09:14,106 --> 00:09:17,196
当然 完全由您做主 首相
Well, it's entirely up to you, of course, Prime Minister,

182
00:09:17,231 --> 00:09:21,194
不过我怀疑女王陛下会有点意外
but I suspect Her Majesty might be a little surprised

183
00:09:21,195 --> 00:09:23,644
如果您要她任命
if you asked her to appoint a man who'd

184
00:09:23,679 --> 00:09:26,809
一个让她打破加冕时"捍卫国教"誓言的人
make her break her coronation vows to defend the Church

185
00:09:27,353 --> 00:09:28,759
那干吗把他列进来?
Why's he on the list, then?

186
00:09:29,335 --> 00:09:33,449
他也不完全是政教分离派
Well, he's not quite a disestablishmentarian yet.

187
00:09:33,484 --> 00:09:36,654
可他的思想似乎有这个趋向
But that's the way his mind seems to be moving.

188
00:09:36,689 --> 00:09:36,947
明白了
I see.

189
00:09:36,948 --> 00:09:41,118
所以我得选麦克史丹弗或麦克史丹弗?
So I'm being asked to choose Mike Stanford or Mike Stanford?

190
00:09:41,691 --> 00:09:44,004
首相 委员会已经
Prime Minister, The Commission is offering you

191
00:09:44,005 --> 00:09:45,839
提名了两个候选人
the two names which emerged

192
00:09:45,910 --> 00:09:47,500
自由选举出来的?
Was there an open election?

193
00:09:47,501 --> 00:09:51,718
不可能 主教遵从使徒递袭
No. Bishops are in the apostolic succession.

194
00:09:51,753 --> 00:09:53,125
什么意思?      上帝的旨意
What's that?        It's God's will.

195
00:09:55,028 --> 00:09:59,074
当初犹大堕落之后 就要换人
When Judas Iscariot blotted his copybook, he was replaced.

196
00:09:59,075 --> 00:10:00,714
他们让圣灵决定
They let the Holy Ghost decide.

197
00:10:01,411 --> 00:10:05,446
圣灵怎么传达旨意?      抓阄
How did he make his views known?        By drawing lots.

198
00:10:07,316 --> 00:10:09,954
这次不能让圣灵决定吗?
Couldn't we let the Holy Ghost decide this time?

199
00:10:09,989 --> 00:10:12,200
没人相信圣灵知道
No one's confident the Holy Ghost would know

200
00:10:12,201 --> 00:10:13,894
英国圣公会主教的条件
what makes a good Church of England bishop.

201
00:10:14,931 --> 00:10:19,129
汉弗莱爵士快到了 首相 能明天再谈吗?
Sir Humphrey is due here now. Could we continue tomorrow?

202
00:10:19,291 --> 00:10:21,885
没问题 谢谢 首相
Not at all. Thank you, Prime Minister.

203
00:10:22,051 --> 00:10:26,051
首相 任命史丹弗
Prime Minister, appointing Canon Stanford

204
00:10:26,052 --> 00:10:27,103
可能会自摆乌龙
may be an own goal

205
00:10:27,138 --> 00:10:28,641
我去调他的履历好吗?
May I get his career details?

206
00:10:28,741 --> 00:10:30,982
好 谢谢      我叫汉弗莱爵士进来
Yes, please do.        And I'll send Sir Humphrey in.

207
00:10:36,999 --> 00:10:41,278
伯纳 首相      汉弗莱 要雪利酒吗?
Bernard. Prime Minister.        Ah, Humphrey. Sherry?

208
00:10:41,313 --> 00:10:43,427
好的 谢谢
Yes, thank you.

209
00:10:45,651 --> 00:10:49,285
汉弗莱 圣公会的现代派是什么意思?
What's a modernist in the Church of England?

210
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,789
这个嘛 "现代派"指不信教的人
Ah, well, the word ''modernist'' is code for non-believer.

211
00:10:55,402 --> 00:10:57,673
你说无神论者?      不不 首相
You mean an atheist?        No, no.Prime Minister

212
00:10:57,708 --> 00:11:00,830
无神论者拿不到教会津贴
An atheist couldn't continue to draw his stipend,

213
00:11:01,331 --> 00:11:03,123
所以当他们不信上帝了
so when they stop believing in God

214
00:11:03,124 --> 00:11:04,854
就自称现代派
they call themselves modernists.

215
00:11:06,412 --> 00:11:07,405
圣公会怎能
How could the Church of England

216
00:11:07,406 --> 00:11:10,219
推荐无神论者当主教?
suggest an atheist as bishop

217
00:11:10,254 --> 00:11:11,241
很简单
They are easy.

218
00:11:11,242 --> 00:11:13,914
圣公会主要是个社会团体
The Church of England is primarily a social organisation,

219
00:11:13,915 --> 00:11:14,853
不是宗教团体
not religious.

220
00:11:14,888 --> 00:11:19,376
是吗?      对 我国多样社会结构的一部分
Is it?        Part of the rich social fabric of the country.

221
00:11:19,411 --> 00:11:21,797
主教要谈吐得体 礼数周全
Bishops need to be the sort of chaps who speak properly,

222
00:11:21,798 --> 00:11:23,801
懂得选用刀叉
know which knife and fork to use.

223
00:11:24,964 --> 00:11:27,116
让人心生敬畏的人物
The sort of people one can look up to.

224
00:11:27,329 --> 00:11:30,858
所以史丹弗教士的夫人特别合适
So Canon Stanford's wife's eminently suitable

225
00:11:30,859 --> 00:11:32,191
当然 干杯
Of course. Cheers.

226
00:11:32,226 --> 00:11:35,649
真没别的候选人了?      不能说有
Is there really no other candidate?        Well, not really.

227
00:11:35,851 --> 00:11:38,220
近来有更好的职位出缺了
There were better jobs available recently.

228
00:11:38,221 --> 00:11:41,234
什么比主教(象棋里的相)还好? 赌棍(车)
What's better than a bishop? A rook?

229
00:11:43,881 --> 00:11:44,974
很好笑
Very droll.

230
00:11:46,531 --> 00:11:49,043
不 温莎教长就是更好的职位
No, Dean of Windsor is a better job.

231
00:11:49,044 --> 00:11:50,310
西敏寺教长也是
Or Westminster.

232
00:11:50,345 --> 00:11:53,783
能使人和皇室亲密起来
It enables one to be on better terms with the Royals.

233
00:11:53,891 --> 00:11:55,926
这么说主教就是个名份喽?
So being a bishop is just a matter of status?

234
00:11:55,927 --> 00:11:58,944
能穿长袍 长统靴
Dressing up in cassocks and gaiters.

235
00:11:58,979 --> 00:12:01,877
对 尽管长统靴只有
Yes, though gaiters are now only worn

236
00:12:01,878 --> 00:12:03,608
在重大宗教场合才穿
at significant religious events

237
00:12:03,643 --> 00:12:05,369
比如皇室游园会
like the Royal garden party.

238
00:12:06,706 --> 00:12:10,264
为什么?      教会想尽量拉近联系
Why?        The Church is trying to be more relevant.

239
00:12:10,299 --> 00:12:13,070
跟上帝?      不 当然不是 首相
To God?        No, of course not. PM.

240
00:12:14,075 --> 00:12:16,390
社会学上的联系
I meant relevant in sociological terms.

241
00:12:16,411 --> 00:12:19,314
那在教会看来
So the ideal candidate in the Church's view

242
00:12:19,315 --> 00:12:22,456
最理想的莫过于一位社会主义社交名流?
is a cross between a socialite and a socialist?

243
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,259
正是
Precisely.

244
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,790
抱歉打扰一下
May I just interrupt.

245
00:12:24,791 --> 00:12:27,472
您要听史丹弗教长的履历吗?
May I give you career details of Dean Conan Stanford?

246
00:12:27,507 --> 00:12:28,067
请说吧
Please do.

247
00:12:28,068 --> 00:12:31,210
神学院毕业后 任设菲尔德助理牧师
He was chaplain to the Bishop of Sheffield.

248
00:12:31,211 --> 00:12:33,817
提拔为教区
He moved on to be the diocesan advisor

249
00:12:33,818 --> 00:12:36,440
异教徒团体与社区顾问
on ethnic communities and social responsibility.

250
00:12:36,475 --> 00:12:39,432
组织过各种不同信仰交流会
He organised conferences on inter-faith interface

251
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:42,775
基督徒和马克思主义者
and inter-faith between Christians and Marxists,and

252
00:12:42,810 --> 00:12:44,868
基督徒和格林汉芒左派反战妇女营
between Christians and the women of Greenham Common

253
00:12:46,211 --> 00:12:49,973
他曾任埃塞克斯大学牧师
He was chaplain at the University of Essex,

254
00:12:49,974 --> 00:12:52,171
神学院副院长
vice-principal at a theological college

255
00:12:52,206 --> 00:12:54,976
现任教会理事会
and is now secretary to the Disarmament Committee

256
00:12:54,977 --> 00:12:56,875
裁军委员会干事
of the Council of Churches.

257
00:12:56,910 --> 00:12:59,307
他当过普通教区牧师吗?
Has he ever been an ordinary vicar of a parish?

258
00:13:00,171 --> 00:13:02,429
天啊 没有 首相
Good heavens, no. PM.

259
00:13:02,430 --> 00:13:03,709
想当主教的神职人员
Clergymen who want to be bishops

260
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:05,289
总要回避教区工作
try to avoid pastoral work.

261
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:09,543
你是说 他是个政坛刺头?
So you're saying he's a political troublemaker?

262
00:13:09,578 --> 00:13:12,325
不 不过他可能阻碍您处理社会问题
No, but he could be a thorn in your side on social issues

263
00:13:12,326 --> 00:13:15,328
罢工 公共福利开支
strikes, public expenditure on welfare,

264
00:13:15,363 --> 00:13:17,461
内城建设 就业 国防之类问题
inner cities, unemployment, defence.

265
00:13:17,491 --> 00:13:19,909
有意思吧 如今
It's interesting that nowadays

266
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:22,737
政客们喜欢拿道德说事
politicians want to talk about moral issues

267
00:13:22,772 --> 00:13:24,457
主教们却忙着谈政治
and bishops want to talk politics.

268
00:13:25,091 --> 00:13:27,359
他还会拥有主教和
And he'd speak with the authority of a bishop

269
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,239
上院议员的话语权
and from the Lords.

270
00:13:29,274 --> 00:13:31,631
他设计过南伦敦一座教堂
He designed a new church in South London

271
00:13:31,666 --> 00:13:33,703
专门设有橙汁供应区
with places for dispensing orange juice,

272
00:13:33,704 --> 00:13:35,638
家庭区 示威组织区
family planning and organising demos...

273
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:41,575
却没地方主持圣餐      你说真的?
But no place for Holy Communion.        Are you serious?

274
00:13:41,610 --> 00:13:44,732
倒有一个两用厅
Well, there was a dual-purpose hall.

275
00:13:45,154 --> 00:13:46,291
教会就批准啦?
And the Church approved this?

276
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:50,637
当然 教会由神学家管理      所以呢?
Of course. The Church is run by theologians.        So?

277
00:13:50,672 --> 00:13:54,354
神学是把不可知论者
Well, theology is a device for enabling agnostics

278
00:13:54,355 --> 00:13:55,647
留在教会内的手段
to stay within the Church.

279
00:13:56,928 --> 00:13:58,952
我不想要史丹弗 我该怎么办?
I don't want Stanford. What am I to do?

280
00:13:58,987 --> 00:14:02,017
您可以两个都拒绝
You could turn both candidates down,

281
00:14:02,018 --> 00:14:04,945
可这就开了特例 我们不推荐
but that would be exceptional and not advised.

282
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:07,555
就算一个候选人想把上帝赶出教会
Even though one wants God out of the Church of England

283
00:14:07,556 --> 00:14:09,142
另一个想赶走女王?
and the other wants the Queen out?

284
00:14:10,211 --> 00:14:12,421
女王和教会不可分离
The Queen is inseparable from the Church.

285
00:14:12,422 --> 00:14:14,128
上帝呢?
What about God?

286
00:14:15,651 --> 00:14:18,449
我想他就是所谓"附加选项"
I think he's what's called an optional extra.

287
00:14:23,007 --> 00:14:26,823
伯纳马上过来 那护士有消息吗?
Bernard's on his way up. Any more news about that nurse?

288
00:14:26,858 --> 00:14:28,319
没 没什么消息
No, not really.

289
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:30,456
外交部没办法吗?
Can't the Foreign Office do something?

290
00:14:30,491 --> 00:14:33,080
外交部不是想办法的
The Foreign Office is there to explain

291
00:14:33,015 --> 00:14:34,619
是解释为什么没办法的
why things can't be done.

292
00:14:35,211 --> 00:14:37,600
这可能严重损害政府
This could damage us very badly.

293
00:14:37,771 --> 00:14:40,067
外交部只会耸耸肩
All the Foreign Office does is shrug

294
00:14:40,068 --> 00:14:42,235
解释我们惹不起库朗人
and say we mustn't upset the Kumranis.

295
00:14:42,331 --> 00:14:45,403
她一定很害怕      谁?
Must be ghastly for her.        Who?

296
00:14:45,611 --> 00:14:48,062
哦 那个护士 对
Oh, that nurse. Yes.

297
00:14:49,293 --> 00:14:52,447
你不比外交部在乎她      哦 安妮
You don't care about her either.        Oh, Annie.

298
00:14:53,492 --> 00:14:56,219
你只在乎你的支持率
You're only worried about your popularity.

299
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:57,227
胡说
That's not true.

300
00:14:57,371 --> 00:15:00,069
抱歉 首相 出了大事
Sorry, Prime Minister. It's rather important.

301
00:15:00,091 --> 00:15:01,584
外交部来电话说
The Foreign Office just right to say

302
00:15:01,585 --> 00:15:04,024
班伯里主教和教会传道会
The Bishop of Banbury and the Church Missionary Society

303
00:15:04,251 --> 00:15:06,373
宣布他们派贝利学院教务长
are sending the Dean of Baillie College to

304
00:15:06,374 --> 00:15:08,978
去库朗执行仁慈使命 拯救护士
Kumran on a mercy mission.

305
00:15:09,013 --> 00:15:10,698
牛津的教师? 为什么?
An Oxford don? Why?

306
00:15:10,699 --> 00:15:13,442
他是基督徒 也是伊斯兰教专家
He is a Christian. He's an expert on Islam.

307
00:15:13,477 --> 00:15:15,516
这是教会跟教会碰头
It's a faith to faith meeting.

308
00:15:17,494 --> 00:15:18,131
好 伯纳
All right. Bernard

309
00:15:18,132 --> 00:15:21,025
告诉外交部我支持他们支持他
Tell the Foreign Office I support their moves to support him

310
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:23,173
不 外交部想请您阻止
No, the Foreign Office want you to stop it.

311
00:15:24,806 --> 00:15:26,336
他们说这是无用功
They say it's a futile gesture

312
00:15:26,337 --> 00:15:28,974
只会损害两国友好关系
which will impair our relationship with a friendly country.

313
00:15:29,009 --> 00:15:31,458
我才不阻止呢 我觉得是好办法
I am not going to stop it. But I think it's a good idea.

314
00:15:31,459 --> 00:15:32,207
对吧 安妮?
Don't you, Annie?

315
00:15:32,242 --> 00:15:33,538
你是说可能救出护士?
You mean it might save the nurse?

316
00:15:33,539 --> 00:15:35,815
对 也有这原因
Er, yes, that too.

317
00:15:36,371 --> 00:15:39,545
首要目标 好 叫他们放手去做
Principally. All right, tell them to go ahead.

318
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:41,380
坎特伯雷大主教问您
Oh, Lambeth Palace want to know

319
00:15:41,381 --> 00:15:43,712
圣埃德蒙的事定了没
if you've decided about Bury St Edmunds.

320
00:15:43,747 --> 00:15:45,562
好的 伯纳 谢谢      晚安
All right, Bernard. Thank you.        Good night.

321
00:15:46,919 --> 00:15:48,422
圣埃德蒙的什么事?
What's happening in Bury St Edmunds?

322
00:15:48,457 --> 00:15:52,267
要我选个主教      真可笑
I've got to choose a bishop.        That's ridiculous!

323
00:15:52,302 --> 00:15:55,839
为什么?      你不大信教吧 亲爱的
Why?        You're not exactly religious.

324
00:15:55,851 --> 00:15:58,823
我是首相 宗教跟这无关
I'm Prime Minister. Religion has nothing to do with it.

325
00:16:00,216 --> 00:16:02,152
跟主教无关?      基本无关
To do with bishops?        Not really.

326
00:16:02,171 --> 00:16:05,495
他们就是经理 穿得花哨而已
They're just managers in fancy dress.

327
00:16:06,968 --> 00:16:10,760
圣公会有17.2万亩地产
The Church of England has over 172,000 acres of land,

328
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:12,494
数千佃户
thousands of tenants,

329
00:16:12,529 --> 00:16:15,893
租赁权 产权和投资
leaseholds, property and investments

330
00:16:15,894 --> 00:16:18,902
总值达16亿镑
worth a total of 1.6 billion pounds.

331
00:16:19,578 --> 00:16:21,559
理想的主教是个集团公司经理
The ideal bishop is a corporate executive.

332
00:16:21,594 --> 00:16:23,273
兼任银行家
A sort of merchant banker,

333
00:16:23,274 --> 00:16:25,495
人事主管和不动产经济人
personnel manager and estate agent.

334
00:16:26,071 --> 00:16:29,264
我希望你选个笃信上帝的
I'd prefer you to choose a man of God.

335
00:16:29,299 --> 00:16:30,991
他们推荐了一个
They offered me one of those,

336
00:16:30,992 --> 00:16:33,865
不过他想把教会变成宗教运动
but he wants to turn the Church into a religious movement.

337
00:16:36,014 --> 00:16:38,481
他们想塞给我一个现代派
They're trying to force a modernist.

338
00:16:38,482 --> 00:16:39,792
左派还是无神论者?
Marxist or atheist?

339
00:16:39,827 --> 00:16:42,529
都是 无神论者倒不要紧
Both. Doesn't matter about the atheist bit,

340
00:16:42,691 --> 00:16:45,588
可左派就麻烦了
but being a Marxist could cause me a lot of trouble

341
00:16:45,589 --> 00:16:48,158
他要在上院演讲的
once he's in the House of Lords.

342
00:16:48,193 --> 00:16:50,978
不能否决他吗?      会显得像搞政治的
Can't you turn him down?        It would look political.

343
00:16:51,451 --> 00:16:54,517
你说教会就是搞政治的嘛
You said the Church IS political.

344
00:16:54,518 --> 00:16:55,870
可不能显出来
But it mustn't look it.

345
00:16:55,905 --> 00:16:57,625
明白了
I see.

346
00:16:57,891 --> 00:17:01,592
干嘛不用宗教原因排除他?
Why not turn him down on religious grounds?

347
00:17:01,593 --> 00:17:02,536
怎么讲?
How do you mean?

348
00:17:02,571 --> 00:17:05,935
他相信有天堂地狱吗?      当然不信
Does he believe in Heaven and Hell?        Of course not.

349
00:17:05,970 --> 00:17:08,475
圣灵感孕呢? 神子复活呢?
The virgin birth? The resurrection?

350
00:17:08,476 --> 00:17:09,808
不 这些都不信
No, nothing like that.

351
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:14,851
那还不够?      安妮 你太聪明了
Isn't that enough?        Annie, you're brilliant!

352
00:17:15,131 --> 00:17:19,124
我要两个都否决 逼他们再提一个
I'll reject both candidates and force them to submit another

353
00:17:19,291 --> 00:17:22,920
我想要的是大家都接受的人
I really want a candidate who'll get on with everybody.

354
00:17:23,131 --> 00:17:26,464
对什么都没主意的?      对
Someone without strong views on anything?        Yes.

355
00:17:27,291 --> 00:17:30,557
如果有基督教倾向也许更好
It might help if he were inclined towards Christianity.

356
00:17:31,966 --> 00:17:33,258
反正没坏处
That wouldn't do any real harm.

357
00:17:33,731 --> 00:17:37,226
那你真正需要的是个秘密基督徒
So what you need is a sort of closet Christian.

358
00:17:37,586 --> 00:17:40,281
正是 谢谢 亲爱的
Exactly. Thank you, darling.

359
00:17:44,669 --> 00:17:47,044
BBC晚间新闻
The Six 0'Clock News from the BBC,

360
00:17:47,045 --> 00:17:49,629
苏罗雷和尼古拉威彻播出
with Sue Lawley and Nicholas Witchell.

361
00:17:51,992 --> 00:17:52,838
晚上好
Good evening.

362
00:17:52,839 --> 00:17:56,072
最新消息 经过在库朗两周的磋商
News is just coming in that after two weeks in Kumran

363
00:17:56,107 --> 00:18:00,318
贝利学院教务长成功
the Dean of Baillie College has succeeded

364
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:02,867
释放了菲奥娜麦格
in obtaining the release of Fiona McGregor,

365
00:18:02,902 --> 00:18:04,984
被捕下狱的英国护士
the British nurse held there in prison.

366
00:18:05,798 --> 00:18:08,779
早先她因持有一瓶威士忌
She was awaiting a sentence of 40 lashes

367
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:11,644
被判40下鞭刑
for possessing a bottle of whisky.

368
00:18:11,679 --> 00:18:15,343
她和教务长定于明天回国
She and the Dean are expected back in England tomorrow.

369
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,941
下面是其它新闻
Now for the rest of the news.

370
00:18:16,976 --> 00:18:19,280
今日英镑汇率仍然不妙
The pound had another bad day...

371
00:18:20,851 --> 00:18:24,862
是真的啊 真不敢相信
So it's true. I can't believe it.

372
00:18:24,897 --> 00:18:27,946
灾难啊      灾难
It's a disaster.        Disaster!

373
00:18:28,211 --> 00:18:31,791
谁的馊主意 派他去库朗的?
Whose idea was it to send him to Kumran?

374
00:18:31,826 --> 00:18:34,695
这可难说 班伯里主教吧?
Eh, can't imagine. Bishop of Banbury perhaps?

375
00:18:35,482 --> 00:18:37,801
外交部本来都控制局势了
We had the situation under control.

376
00:18:37,802 --> 00:18:39,828
那还用说
Yes, of course you did.

377
00:18:41,052 --> 00:18:42,633
我们提了抗议
We made our protest.

378
00:18:42,634 --> 00:18:44,662
护士会悄悄挨鞭子
The nurse would have been quietly flogged and

379
00:18:44,663 --> 00:18:46,743
塞到牢里去
stuffed in some jail.

380
00:18:48,545 --> 00:18:52,304
不出几周 媒体就忘光了
Within a couple of weeks, the press would forget.

381
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,786
好在没什么实际损失
Still, no real damage done.

382
00:18:53,787 --> 00:18:55,737
外交部损失重大啊
There is to the Foreign Office.

383
00:18:56,171 --> 00:18:58,183
他们都快同意
We've almost got agreement to

384
00:18:58,184 --> 00:19:00,765
我们在库朗设个监听站了
set up a signals listening post in Kumran.

385
00:19:00,801 --> 00:19:03,412
我们说他们答应 我们就不纠缠护士的事
We said we wouldn't make a fuss if they signed.

386
00:19:04,065 --> 00:19:06,583
这下最大的筹码没了
We've lost our best bargaining counter.

387
00:19:06,618 --> 00:19:09,463
你们总可以再找个护士 栽瓶威士忌嘛
You could find another nurse and plant some Scotch on her!

388
00:19:11,279 --> 00:19:12,693
这我们可办不到
I don't think we could do that.

389
00:19:14,110 --> 00:19:16,068
对对 这样不好
No. No, it wouldn't be right.

390
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:19,138
不 风险太大了
No, it's too dangerous.

391
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:25,086
不过 至少帮我把她该死的母亲摆脱了
at least it's got that nurse's ghastly mother off my back

392
00:19:26,262 --> 00:19:29,312
她一个劲写信 打电话 跟媒体
She's been writing and phoning and telling the press

393
00:19:29,313 --> 00:19:31,224
说我们袖手旁观
that we haven't been doing anything.

394
00:19:31,259 --> 00:19:35,213
真过分      媒体还都向着她
Extraordinary.        And the press have taken her part.

395
00:19:35,248 --> 00:19:38,765
说什么我们不爱国      太过分了
Going on about being more patriotic!        Extraordinary.

396
00:19:38,971 --> 00:19:42,138
他们说过外交部不少坏话
They've said a lot of unpleasant things,

397
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:44,508
可从没骂我们不爱国
but we've never been accused of patriotism!

398
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:51,050
有时我真难相信
Sometimes I can't believe the newspapers'

399
00:19:51,051 --> 00:19:51,764
报界对外交局势这么无知
abject ignorance of diplomatic realities.

400
00:19:51,799 --> 00:19:54,846
可我们对首相不好交待了
But we may have a problem with the PM now.

401
00:19:54,931 --> 00:19:58,092
因为我们反对他派牧师?
Because we advised him against this?

402
00:19:58,127 --> 00:20:00,284
还因为你让外交部长说
Because the Foreign Secretary said

403
00:20:00,285 --> 00:20:02,817
释放她办不到
it was impossible to get her released!

404
00:20:02,852 --> 00:20:05,610
我们没错 如果交给外交部
And we were right! If we'd left it to the Foreign Office

405
00:20:05,645 --> 00:20:07,071
绝对办不到
it would have been impossible.

406
00:20:08,051 --> 00:20:09,922
知道会怎样了吧
You see what will happen now?

407
00:20:09,923 --> 00:20:13,367
媒体会说教会能力强过外交部
The press will say the Church succeeds where the F.O. fails.

408
00:20:13,402 --> 00:20:15,620
又会翻出老一套
They'll dig out all the old cuttings

409
00:20:15,621 --> 00:20:17,479
大使的豪华轿车
about ambassadors' Rolls Royces,

410
00:20:17,971 --> 00:20:19,874
400万镑的大使馆
4 million embassies,

411
00:20:19,875 --> 00:20:22,754
纳税人代缴的伊顿学费
school fees at Eton paid for by the taxpayer and

412
00:20:22,755 --> 00:20:24,215
英国得到什么?
what does Britain get?

413
00:20:24,250 --> 00:20:27,911
千万别 我有办法了      什么?
Don't. I know what we'll do.        What?

414
00:20:28,847 --> 00:20:31,553
我们告诉媒体 是首相
We'll tell the press that it was the Prime Minister's

415
00:20:31,554 --> 00:20:33,739
作主派教务长的
initiative to send the Dean.

416
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:37,447
好主意 首相就喜欢居功
Good idea. The PM will enjoy taking the credit.

417
00:20:38,051 --> 00:20:42,404
首相不会因为这是撒谎 就不乐意吧?
There's no danger the PM will deny it because it isn't true?

418
00:20:42,611 --> 00:20:44,457
绝对不会
None at all.

419
00:20:46,851 --> 00:20:48,595
再向周日邮报透消息
And then for the Sundays

420
00:20:48,596 --> 00:20:53,394
说是外交部建议首相的
we leak the idea that the Foreign Office suggested it to him

421
00:20:53,429 --> 00:20:56,058
因为外交途径受阻了
when the diplomatic channels were blocked.

422
00:20:56,093 --> 00:20:57,971
完美 这样没人有错
Perfect. Nobody gets the blame and

423
00:20:57,972 --> 00:20:59,445
人人都有功
everybody gets the credit.

424
00:21:00,611 --> 00:21:02,951
除了真想出这点子的人
Except the person who really thought it up.

425
00:21:02,952 --> 00:21:04,379
我不介意
I don't mind.

426
00:21:11,051 --> 00:21:14,857
我不介意他没功劳 不管是谁 抱歉
I don't mind that he doesn't get the credit. Excuse me.

427
00:21:15,211 --> 00:21:17,525
喂 好 接过来
Hello? Oh, put him on.

428
00:21:18,834 --> 00:21:20,555
你好 院长
Oh, hello, Master.

429
00:21:20,590 --> 00:21:23,468
看到电视新闻了吗? 太棒了
Have you seen the television news? Splendid!

430
00:21:23,503 --> 00:21:24,667
对 简直太棒了
Yes, absolutely splendid.

431
00:21:24,668 --> 00:21:27,438
能推我们的朋友一把吧?
This could help our friend, eh?

432
00:21:27,473 --> 00:21:28,106
绝对能
Certainly could.

433
00:21:28,107 --> 00:21:32,266
什么时候有主教出缺?
How long until a bishopric falls vacant?

434
00:21:32,301 --> 00:21:34,205
现在正是时候
Well, there's no time like the present.

435
00:21:34,571 --> 00:21:38,641
我觉得圣埃德蒙之战还没完
I think the battle of Bury St Edmunds is not over yet.

436
00:21:38,642 --> 00:21:41,613
对 我是说过 可又有新动向
I know what I said. There have been developments.

437
00:21:41,648 --> 00:21:43,238
抱歉
Excuse me.

438
00:21:44,091 --> 00:21:48,337
喂 好 请他进来 谢谢
Hello? Yes, ask him to come in. Thank you.

439
00:21:50,223 --> 00:21:54,052
我看还有办法把教务长拉上起跑线
I think we can still get the Dean up to the starting gate.

440
00:21:54,087 --> 00:21:57,052
后发制人 交给我就行了
As a late entry. Just leave it to me.

441
00:21:57,087 --> 00:22:00,006
好的 再见 院长 再见
All right. Bye, Master. Bye-bye.

442
00:22:01,057 --> 00:22:02,330
请进来 彼得
Ah, come in, Peter.

443
00:22:03,629 --> 00:22:05,977
我听说皇室任命委员会
I understand there's a meeting of

444
00:22:05,978 --> 00:22:08,501
明早要开会?
the Crown Appointments Commission in the morning?

445
00:22:08,536 --> 00:22:12,457
对 他们知道了要选新的候选人
Yes, they are aware that a further candidate is required

446
00:22:12,491 --> 00:22:14,985
因为首相觉得有必要打破传统
since the PM saw fit to break with tradition.

447
00:22:15,131 --> 00:22:18,282
你是说 他非要选个信教的主教?
By insisting on a bishop who is a believer?

448
00:22:18,491 --> 00:22:22,666
还有一个候选人 史蒂文萨默
There is one possible candidate, Steven Soames,

449
00:22:22,667 --> 00:22:24,751
我们留了很多年了
but we've saved him up for years.

450
00:22:24,786 --> 00:22:26,445
本打算派他去特鲁罗(英格兰西南)
We'd rather offer him Truro.

451
00:22:26,446 --> 00:22:27,243
为什么?
Why?

452
00:22:27,278 --> 00:22:30,519
特鲁罗...怎么说呢? 比较远
Well, Truro is... How shall I put it? Very remote.

453
00:22:31,949 --> 00:22:34,760
对教会来说 等于斯旺西(威尔士)
It is to the Church what the Vehicle Licensing Centre

454
00:22:34,761 --> 00:22:36,232
车牌管理处对公务员
in Swansea is to the Civil Service.

455
00:22:37,251 --> 00:22:38,697
对啊
Yes.

456
00:22:39,131 --> 00:22:43,780
萨默等了很多年了      好久不见
Soames has been waiting for years.        Long time, no see.

457
00:22:44,931 --> 00:22:47,385
很好笑 汉弗莱
Oh, very droll, Humphrey.

458
00:22:48,451 --> 00:22:50,564
对 他是有点讨厌
Yes, he is a bit of a nuisance.

459
00:22:50,565 --> 00:22:53,699
老叫我们对上帝尽义务
He keeps on about our duty to God and that sort of things

460
00:22:53,734 --> 00:22:58,299
我们想赶走他 "好久不见"
We rather wanted him out of the way. ''Long time, no see''!

461
00:22:59,688 --> 00:23:01,667
对 可如果首相要信教的主教
Yes, but if the PM wants a religious bishop,

462
00:23:01,668 --> 00:23:02,900
他是唯一候选人
he's the only candidate.

463
00:23:02,935 --> 00:23:05,950
对 听起来不错 可有个问题
He sounds fine, but there is one little snag.

464
00:23:05,985 --> 00:23:10,169
首相要两名新候选人      两名?
The PM wants you to put up two more names.        Two?

465
00:23:10,204 --> 00:23:13,059
对 你得让首相觉得有选择余地
You must give the PM the feeling of a choice.

466
00:23:13,094 --> 00:23:16,099
你得再找个候选人 貌似合理
You need a second candidate who is plausible,

467
00:23:16,100 --> 00:23:17,443
但不可能的
but unacceptable.

468
00:23:17,478 --> 00:23:20,198
我想不到 明早就开会了
I can't think who and the meeting's so soon.

469
00:23:20,199 --> 00:23:23,222
贝利学院教务长不行吗?
Why not the Dean of Baillie College?

470
00:23:23,257 --> 00:23:27,712
他确实不可能 但也不合理啊
I agree he is impossible, but not plausible.

471
00:23:27,747 --> 00:23:28,614
怎么讲?
Why not?

472
00:23:28,649 --> 00:23:29,735
他是个怪人
He's a crank!

473
00:23:30,647 --> 00:23:33,978
极其自负 又无能得不像话
He's unbelievably vain and hopelessly incompetent.

474
00:23:34,013 --> 00:23:37,724
对 可首相从不介意任命自负又无能的人
But the PM appoints people who are vain and incompetent

475
00:23:37,725 --> 00:23:38,888
看看内阁
look at the Cabinet.

476
00:23:41,458 --> 00:23:43,679
再说教务长刚刚大出风头
And the Dean's just had good publicity.

477
00:23:44,303 --> 00:23:46,376
那他不是有选上的危险吗?
Isn't there a danger he'll get in?

478
00:23:46,411 --> 00:23:47,663
一点也没有
Not the slightest.

479
00:23:47,664 --> 00:23:51,440
首相说了要虔诚基督徒
The PM has stated that he wants a devout Christian.

480
00:23:51,475 --> 00:23:53,591
教务长只相信伊斯兰教
The Dean only believes in Islam,

481
00:23:53,592 --> 00:23:55,331
蒸汽机和板球俱乐部
steam engines and the MCC.

482
00:23:55,611 --> 00:23:59,343
有次电视节目里
In fact, some smart aleck once asked him on TV

483
00:23:59,344 --> 00:24:00,882
有人问他知不知道圣经是什么
if he knew what the Bible was.

484
00:24:00,917 --> 00:24:02,013
他知道吗?
And did he?

485
00:24:02,014 --> 00:24:05,717
对 他说那是基督教的古兰经
He said it's a Christian version of the Koran.

486
00:24:08,051 --> 00:24:11,647
"吉姆的教务长鞭下拯救菲奥娜"
''Jim's Dean saves Fiona from lash''!

487
00:24:11,682 --> 00:24:13,680
怎么样 汉弗莱?      精彩绝伦 首相
What about that?        Excellent.

488
00:24:13,851 --> 00:24:17,267
"首相特使达成释放"
''Prime Minister's envoy secures release''.

489
00:24:17,268 --> 00:24:18,898
精彩绝伦 首相
Excellent, Prime Minister.

490
00:24:18,933 --> 00:24:22,578
"首相派出仁慈天使"      精彩绝伦 首相
''Angel of mercy was sent by PM''!        Excellent!

491
00:24:22,613 --> 00:24:26,449
昨晚新闻把功劳全归给我 是我干的吧?
I was given full credit on the news. I suppose it was me.

492
00:24:26,651 --> 00:24:28,801
铁板钉钉 报纸都说了
It must have been.

493
00:24:30,297 --> 00:24:33,129
是我不让外交部制止他的
After all, I stopped the Foreign Office from stopping him,

494
00:24:33,130 --> 00:24:34,238
一回事嘛
which is the same thing.

495
00:24:34,273 --> 00:24:36,035
现在想改也晚了
Too late to change it now.

496
00:24:36,036 --> 00:24:40,477
我还是不明白 外交部为什么归功于我
I wonder why they gave me the credit, though.

497
00:24:40,512 --> 00:24:43,305
反正他们自己也占不了
Well, they couldn't take it themselves.

498
00:24:43,306 --> 00:24:45,398
这样说起来像政府成就
This looks like a government achievement.

499
00:24:45,433 --> 00:24:46,657
看 还有社论呢
There's even a leader.

500
00:24:46,915 --> 00:24:48,774
"首相居功至伟
''It does the PM great credit that

501
00:24:48,775 --> 00:24:52,823
正因为他未受外交锁链束缚"
he has not been bound by the shackles of diplomacy.

502
00:24:53,011 --> 00:24:55,353
"库朗事件..." 这很重要的
''The Kumran aff...'' This is important.

503
00:24:55,388 --> 00:24:58,273
对 可大主教在等您
Yes, but the Palace is waiting for your recommendation

504
00:24:58,274 --> 00:25:00,214
提名圣埃德蒙主教
for Bury St Edmunds.

505
00:25:00,249 --> 00:25:02,437
两个名字昨晚放您文件盒里了
The two names were in your box.

506
00:25:02,691 --> 00:25:05,490
我觉得史蒂芬萨默貌似不错
I thought Steven Soames sounded right.

507
00:25:05,651 --> 00:25:09,027
彼得也说不错 贝利教务长在库朗立了功
The Dean of Baillie did a very good job,

508
00:25:09,028 --> 00:25:10,484
可我听说他是个怪人
but I gather he's rather eccentric.

509
00:25:10,571 --> 00:25:12,573
我肯定萨默是
I'm sure that Soames is

510
00:25:12,574 --> 00:25:15,883
皇家委员会希望您选的人
the choice the Commissioners are hoping you make.

511
00:25:15,918 --> 00:25:17,716
怎么? 他有什么问题?
Oh? Why? What's wrong with him?

512
00:25:19,472 --> 00:25:22,440
这个 我听说他是极端主义者
Well, I have heard say that he's an extremist.

513
00:25:22,475 --> 00:25:26,653
你是说他信上帝?      极其虔诚 首相
You mean he believes in God?        He's very religious.

514
00:25:26,851 --> 00:25:29,057
主教应该这样的吧?
That's all right for a bishop, isn't it?

515
00:25:29,411 --> 00:25:31,231
他倾向于提出
He tends to raise issues

516
00:25:31,232 --> 00:25:34,025
政府想回避的议题
that governments would prefer not to be raised.

517
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:35,814
他尖锐批判未成年人堕胎
He's a trenchant critic of abortion,

518
00:25:35,815 --> 00:25:40,142
避孕 性教育 色情业
contraception under 16, sex education, pornography,

519
00:25:40,177 --> 00:25:43,183
周日商业行为 便利离婚和银幕脏话
Sunday trading, easy divorce and bad language on TV.

520
00:25:43,218 --> 00:25:47,693
他很可能挑战所有这些政策
He'd be likely to challenge government policy.

521
00:25:47,728 --> 00:25:48,774
可这些议题
But these are subjects on which

522
00:25:48,874 --> 00:25:50,590
政府不想出台政策
the government is hoping to have no policy.

523
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:55,507
我们的政策就是无政策
Our policy is not to have a policy.

524
00:25:56,051 --> 00:25:59,778
没错 他就是反对您的无政策政策
Well, quite. He's against your no-policy policy.

525
00:26:00,491 --> 00:26:04,325
他会要求您禁止堕胎 禁止周日交易...
He will demand that you ban abortion, Sunday trading...

526
00:26:04,531 --> 00:26:06,667
谢谢 伯纳 我明白了
Thank you. I get the picture.

527
00:26:07,051 --> 00:26:10,396
他还反对非洲的剥削与压迫
He's also against oppression in Africa.

528
00:26:10,397 --> 00:26:11,253
我们也反对
So are we.

529
00:26:11,288 --> 00:26:14,890
对 可不光白人政府 黑人政府他也反对
But he's against it from black AND white governments.

530
00:26:15,091 --> 00:26:17,213
哦 你说他是种族主义者?
Oh. You mean he's a racist?

531
00:26:20,203 --> 00:26:21,903
可您想选他也可以选
But you can choose him if you like.

532
00:26:23,221 --> 00:26:25,291
我不能再否决两个候选人
I can't turn down another two names.

533
00:26:26,091 --> 00:26:29,174
总还有贝利教务长嘛
Well, there is always the Dean of Baillie.

534
00:26:29,209 --> 00:26:31,111
他不能真算数吧?
He's not really up to it, is he?

535
00:26:31,112 --> 00:26:35,227
我听说他又懒又自负 还对基督教不感兴趣
I gather he's lazy, vain and uninterested in Christianity.

536
00:26:35,262 --> 00:26:37,060
可他也不反对啊
But he's not against it!

537
00:26:38,491 --> 00:26:43,087
我觉得他会是完美的英国主教
I think he would make a thoroughly suitable British bishop.

538
00:26:43,251 --> 00:26:44,792
喜欢板球 蒸汽机 
Cricket, steam engines and 

539
00:26:44,793 --> 00:26:46,795
对神学一无所知
a complete ignorance of theology.

540
00:26:47,731 --> 00:26:52,119
他从没任过教职 一辈子待在牛津
He's never had an ordinary church job. He's been at Oxford.

541
00:26:52,154 --> 00:26:54,370
可他在库朗干的不错      对
But he did well in Kumran.        Yes.

542
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:58,277
我今早听说 他想告诉媒体
I gather he's thinking of telling the press

543
00:26:58,278 --> 00:27:00,328
库朗之行不是您的主意
that the Kumran visit wasn't your idea.

544
00:27:01,533 --> 00:27:05,322
什么?      他想告诉媒体...
What?        He's thinking of telling the press...

545
00:27:05,531 --> 00:27:09,113
对对 我听见了 他不能这么说
Yes, yes, I heard what you said. He can't say that!

546
00:27:09,811 --> 00:27:12,702
我听说他有班伯里主教的信
I gather he has a letter from the Bishop of Banbury

547
00:27:12,703 --> 00:27:15,280
在您介入前发出的
dated before your involvement.

548
00:27:15,315 --> 00:27:17,063
可那就太丢人了
But that would be frightfully embarrassing!

549
00:27:17,064 --> 00:27:20,022
好像我硬揽别人的功似的
Taking credit for something I didn't do.

550
00:27:20,057 --> 00:27:21,617
对 我能预见头条
Yes, I can see the headlines now.

551
00:27:21,618 --> 00:27:26,261
"教务长仁慈使命首相居功"
''PM takes credit for Dean's mercy mission''.

552
00:27:26,296 --> 00:27:29,770
"吉姆没能搞定" 抱歉
''Jim didn't fix it!'' Sorry.

553
00:27:29,805 --> 00:27:32,337
得制止他 怎么才能制止他?
He must be stopped! How can we stop him?

554
00:27:32,338 --> 00:27:35,369
首相 据说他嫌认可不够...
He feels he hasn't had enough recognition...

555
00:27:35,404 --> 00:27:38,894
教会在库朗一事中
That the Church hasn't had enough recognition

556
00:27:38,895 --> 00:27:40,563
得到的认可不够
for its role in Kumran.

557
00:27:40,598 --> 00:27:41,817
那就给他啊
Well, give him some.

558
00:27:41,818 --> 00:27:45,190
今晚请他来喝酒 让媒体拍照
Get him round for drinks. Photo opportunity for the press.

559
00:27:45,225 --> 00:27:47,365
这也许不大合适      为什么?
That might be a little improper.        Why?

560
00:27:47,571 --> 00:27:51,121
您在考虑两个候选人
If you're considering two candidates,

561
00:27:51,156 --> 00:27:54,084
总不能只请一个来喝酒吧
you can hardly invite just one round for a drink.

562
00:27:54,119 --> 00:27:55,888
明白了      除非 当然...
I see.        Unless, of course...

563
00:27:57,091 --> 00:28:00,891
如果您已经任命了他
If you'd already given him the job,

564
00:28:00,892 --> 00:28:03,020
那就非常恰当了
then it would be perfectly proper.

565
00:28:07,651 --> 00:28:09,495
说实话 汉弗莱
Actually, Humphrey,

566
00:28:10,211 --> 00:28:14,027
我觉得贝利教务长当主教不错
I think he's rather a good choice for bishop.

567
00:28:14,062 --> 00:28:17,147
真的 他这人有魄力      魄力
He's an enterprising chap.        Enterprising.

568
00:28:17,182 --> 00:28:19,452
古怪也可以是优点
Eccentricity can be a virtue

569
00:28:19,453 --> 00:28:20,997
改叫它个性的话
If you call it individualism.

570
00:28:21,251 --> 00:28:24,350
这就是所谓不规则动词吧 "某人思想独立
It is called the irregular verb. I have an independent mind,

571
00:28:24,351 --> 00:28:26,330
 某人古怪 某人脑子有病"
you are an eccentric, he is round the twist.

572
00:28:27,616 --> 00:28:28,528
抱歉
Sorry.

573
00:28:29,051 --> 00:28:30,631
谢谢 伯纳
Thank you, Bernard.

574
00:28:32,208 --> 00:28:34,781
再说 上院需要他这样的人
Furthermore, we need people like him in the House of Lords.

575
00:28:34,816 --> 00:28:38,035
懂得阿拉伯世界
People who really understand the Arab world.

576
00:28:38,036 --> 00:28:39,388
还有蒸汽机
And steam engines.

577
00:28:39,451 --> 00:28:42,820
对 经过慎重考虑
Yes, on mature consideration,

578
00:28:42,821 --> 00:28:44,934
我决定选贝利教务长
I think the Dean of Baillie is my choice.

579
00:28:44,969 --> 00:28:47,379
通报大主教 伯纳
Convey that to the Palace, Bernard.

580
00:28:47,414 --> 00:28:48,226
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

581
00:28:48,227 --> 00:28:51,955
马上 赶快 让媒体中午发布
Now! Fast. Announce it by midday.

582
00:28:51,990 --> 00:28:55,122
让他6点来喝酒 快去
Get him round for a drinkie at six. Move!

583
00:28:56,331 --> 00:28:59,359
依我之见 明智的决定 首相
A wise decision, if I may say so. PM

584
00:28:59,360 --> 00:29:00,230
没错 汉弗莱
You may, Humphrey.

585
00:29:01,571 --> 00:29:04,431
你怎么这么了解贝利教务长?
How come you know so much about the Dean of Baillie?

586
00:29:04,432 --> 00:29:07,117
你不是贝利毕业的吗?
Weren't you at Baillie yourself?

587
00:29:07,152 --> 00:29:11,453
没错 我是      替老朋友办事吧?
I was, yes.        Jobs for the boys, is it?

588
00:29:11,611 --> 00:29:14,848
恰恰相反 首相 我们都算不上认识
On the contrary! I hardly know him.

589
00:29:14,883 --> 00:29:17,752
说实话 我刚好知道他不喜欢我
In fact, I happen to know that he dislikes me.

590
00:29:17,787 --> 00:29:20,617
您可以今晚亲自问他
You can ask him yourself this evening.

591
00:29:20,652 --> 00:29:23,377
我也不太喜欢他
I don't like him very much, either.

592
00:29:23,412 --> 00:29:26,001
真的?      以荣誉担保
Honestly?        On my word of honour.

593
00:29:26,036 --> 00:29:30,721
你真无利可图?      怎么会有呢?
You have nothing to gain?        How could I have?

594
00:29:31,846 --> 00:29:33,270
要这么说 干得好
In that case, well done.

595
00:29:33,305 --> 00:29:36,124
有益而无私的建议
Helpful, impartial advice.

596
00:29:36,125 --> 00:29:38,649
公务员系统最优良的传统
The best traditions of the Civil Service.

597
00:29:40,992 --> 00:29:42,276
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

598
00:29:44,372 --> 00:29:54,570
